  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Nameplate decorations create too much visual noise, and make it harder to read text on nameplates. I play with nameplates off most of the time because I find them to be too distracting and ruin the immersion. When I bring up nameplates using the quick menu, it's because I want to be able to read information as quickly as possible, i.e usernames, statues, group banners. Nameplate decorations make this harder, as I now need to visually separate the text from the now differently colored backgrounds. \n\nProfile decorations are already obnoxious on discord, but at the very least they are only visible when you look at someone's profile. I think that as long as VRC keeps profile decorations to user's profile pages, I'm okay with it. Putting it on nameplates takes it too far.",
